support/hardware/DECISION.md:7: The read-only probe ran in the execution-tool Linux container, NOT on a user-provided bare-metal GPU host. Visible environment: Linux 6.18.44, x86_64, virtual CPU model AMD EPYC 9V74 80-Core Processor (3 visible /proc/cpuinfo processor entries, not a claim about physical cores). PCI enumeration exposed host bridge 8086:0d57 and six VirtIO functions: 1af4:1042, 1af4:1041, 1af4:1044, 1af4:105b, 1af4:1053, 1af4:1045. No visible PCI display or compute-accelerator class, NVIDIA or AMD GPU, /dev/dri/renderD128, /dev/kfd, /dev/nvidiactl, /dev/nvidia0, /dev/vfio/vfio or /dev/kvm. No VMX/SVM flags, visible IOMMU group or DMAR/IVRS table. Absence in a restricted container DOES NOT prove physical host absence.
support/hardware/DECISION.md:49: Proposed compute provenance after eventual success: **host kernel Asterinas-derived Rust**, **VM Linux guest kernel**, **guest process Python GEMM**, **physical RTX 4060**, **guest NVIDIA driver**, **guest NVRTC/CUDA runtime**. No part of that combination has yet been demonstrated here. A05 must bind VM/device ownership to final process identity and revocation; A06 must enforce parent ResourceDomain budgets and recovery executor reserve; A01 must integrate real frames, PCI/IOMMU and correct VMX/SVM backend. Hepta calls existing HOS2/ResourceDomain surfaces, not direct PCI registers.
support/hardware/DECISION.md:56: 4. Implement a minimal but actual VMM with vCPU, VM memory, virtual interrupts, device model, boot and lifecycle, correct Intel VMX vs AMD SVM; AMD SVM is not evidenced in pinned upstream. See ../vmm/GATES.md.
support/hardware/DECISION.md:61: **References:** [fixed Asterinas VMX context](https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/blob/c4b7ed575b7b32773475b194d2ad41fb6d03765b/ostd/src/arch/x86/vm/mod.rs); [OSTD example](https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/blob/c4b7ed575b7b32773475b194d2ad41fb6d03765b/osdk/tests/examples_in_book/write_a_hypervisor_in_100_lines_templates/lib.rs); [VFIO/IOMMU groups](https://docs.kernel.org/driver-api/vfio.html); [Linux DMA](https://docs.kernel.org/core-api/dma-api-howto.html); [CUDA launch](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-driver-api/cuda_driver_api/group__CUDA__EXEC.html).
support/vmm/GATES.md:7: | Intel VMX | ostd/src/arch/x86/vm/mod.rs, context.rs, ept.rs, vmx/ and ostd/src/vm/{gpm_space,guest_mode}.rs provide Intel VMX, EPT, guest context/exit primitives | No Linux boot VMM, PCI GPU passthrough, vCPU scheduling, virt IRQ, device model, recovery qualification |
support/vmm/GATES.md:8: | AMD SVM | No SVM-specific file in pinned x86 vm tree; implementation uses VMX/VMCS | Do not use VMX example as proof of AMD SVM/NPT/VMCB/VMRUN, even though visible virtual CPU is AMD |
support/vmm/GATES.md:12: Execution-tool container: Linux 6.18.44, x86_64, no /dev/kvm, no forwarded vmx/svm flags; NO hypervisor run. Upstream osdk/tests/examples_in_book/write_a_hypervisor_in_100_lines_templates/lib.rs demonstrates a small VMX real-mode guest that prints serial and halts; not a Linux guest VM or a GPU VMM.
support/vmm/GATES.md:16: 1. Discover actual architecture at runtime; reject VMX absent on Intel / SVM absent on AMD. If AMD target is chosen, implement/test SVM instead of attempting VMX commands. No aggressive emulation fallback.
support/vmm/GATES.md:24: Only the above can eventually qualify "local GPU in a Linux guest under a Rust host". QEMU/KVM VM on Linux host or reference VMX snippet is categorically different. Performance and GPU reset behavior remain unmeasured.
